            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0099" n="95" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg95"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9411/60: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-06T19:00:00+09:00">December 6, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 6—9:09 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>663. Department’s 385, December 5, 2 p.m. The Foreign Office today confirmed the
                    accuracy of the statement attributed to Suma but emphasized that the statement
                    presented only an objective fact and that no inference going beyond the text
                    would be warranted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
